{"items":[{"tags":["mediawiki","geshi"],"question_score":6,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":true,"answer_count":4,"is_answered":true,"question_id":4928612,"item_type":"question","score":6,"last_activity_date":1780238635,"creation_date":1297127460,"body":"Is it possible to indent a block of code in MediaWiki using SyntaxHighlight GeSHi?\n\nFor example, I would like the code container below to be aligned with the third-level list\n\n\n\nI have tried wrapping the GeSHi code container with colons (using  MediaWiki&#39;s standard indentation syntax), but that prevents SyntaxHighlight GeSHi from parsing the code correctly.\n\nJust to clarify, I would like to avoid wrapping my code with  as I need proper syntax highlighting.\n\nAny suggestions?\n","excerpt":"Is it possible to indent a block of code in MediaWiki using <span class=\"highlight\">SyntaxHighlight</span> GeSHi? &hellip; * argv)\n{\n    my_function(4, 1, 2, 3);\n    return 0;\n}\n&lt;/source&gt;\n\n\nI have tried wrapping the GeSHi code container with colons (using  MediaWiki&#39;s standard indentation syntax), but that prevents <span class=\"highlight\">SyntaxHighlight</span> &hellip; ","title":"Indenting code in MediaWiki"},{"tags":["wordpress","tooling-recommendation"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":2,"is_answered":false,"question_id":79906424,"item_type":"question","score":0,"last_activity_date":1774976714,"creation_date":1773338020,"body":"I have a wordpress blog that is not hosted on wordpress.com. I am writing a post that has snippets of Python code as well commands that I would like readers type into a shell. It also has output from writing commands the Python REPL. I would like to style these code snippets using standard syntax highlighting, similar to what I get when I type three ` followed by  ,  or  in a GitHub README.\nMy understanding is that the normal way to solve problems like this in WordPress is to get a plugin. But the plugin I see most widely cited online  (SyntaxHighlighter Evolved) is causing problems for me. For example, when I try to create a Python code block like this:\n\nIt gets rendered as:\n\nThat is, the  seems to be treated as a Markdown code for an  tag, and converted to HTML.\nIf I switch the editor from &quot;Visual&quot; to Code&quot; I can write this:\n\n```python\ndef foo():\n    return 0\n```\n\nIf I click &quot;Save&quot; and &quot;Preview&quot; the syntax highlighting works as expected. But as soon as I switch the editor back to &quot;Visual&quot; the code gets auto-formatted like this:\n\ndef foo():\nreturn 0\n\nThe syntax highlighting is still correct, but the code gets left-justified, which is actually a syntax error in Python.\nWhen I google this I see other plugins listed, but they all seem to be abandoned.\nWhat is the best way to style code in WordPress blog posts for sites that are not hosted on wordpress.com?\n","excerpt":"I have a wordpress blog that is not hosted on wordpress.com. I am writing a post that has snippets of Python code as well commands that I would like readers type into a shell. It also has output from  &hellip; ","title":"Best way to style code in WordPress blog posts?"},{"tags":["mediawiki"],"question_score":6,"is_accepted":true,"answer_id":5408219,"is_answered":false,"question_id":5399017,"item_type":"answer","score":4,"last_activity_date":1764560205,"creation_date":1300896468,"body":"Yes, you will need to have ToggleDisplay and SyntaxHighlight GeSHi installed.\nThen on your page add code like this (example for C++):\n\n","excerpt":"Yes, you will need to have ToggleDisplay and <span class=\"highlight\">SyntaxHighlight</span> GeSHi installed. &hellip; -- Put the code here --&gt;\n  &lt;/<span class=\"highlight\">syntaxhighlight</span>&gt;\n&lt;/toggledisplay&gt; &hellip; ","title":"Indentable and collapsable text and code snippets in MediaWiki"},{"tags":["syntax-highlighting","blogger"],"question_score":1,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":4,"is_answered":false,"question_id":7777167,"item_type":"question","score":1,"last_activity_date":1747029497,"creation_date":1318673488,"body":"I&#39;m using SyntaxHighlighter for blogger to format the code snippet I use in my blog. I followed steps given in a blog (http://concise-software.blogspot.com/2010/03/enabling-syntaxhighlighter-in-blogger.html) but then it throws error on page load of my blogger post saying &quot;Can&#39;t find brush for : CSS&quot;\n","excerpt":"I&#39;m using SyntaxHighlighter for blogger to format the code snippet I use in my blog. I followed steps given in a blog (http://concise-software.blogspot.com/2010/03/enabling-syntaxhighlighter-in-blogge &hellip; ","title":"Code formatting SyntaxHighlighter for blogger throws error"},{"tags":["swagger-ui","swashbuckle.aspnetcore"],"question_score":8,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":true,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":true,"question_id":64053444,"item_type":"question","score":8,"last_activity_date":1730295000,"creation_date":1600976945,"body":"I am using Swashbuckle.AspNetCore for a project. The version I started with was 5.5.1 and when rendering results with large bodies (20k json rows), the speed was very reasonable (the data fetch takes 50ms and the rendering took less than a second.  When I upgrade to 5.6.x, the syntax is now highlighted (which looks nice) but slows the rendering of those results to over 20 seconds.  And once rendered, any action on the page that causes a refresh takes 20 seconds until the results are cleared.\nAfter the usual searching, I want to try this solution (deactivating syntaxHighlight).  I&#39;m not sure how to do this via Swashbuckle.AspNetCore.  Any suggestions?\n\n","excerpt":"After the usual searching, I want to try this solution (deactivating <span class=\"highlight\">syntaxHighlight</span>).  I&#39;m not sure how to do this via Swashbuckle.AspNetCore.  Any suggestions? &hellip; SwaggerUI({\n        <span class=\"highlight\">syntaxHighlight</span>: {\n          activated: false,\n          theme: &quot;agate&quot;\n        },\n        //url: path,\n        ....\n      }); &hellip; ","title":"Setting syntaxHighlight property for Swagger UI with Swashbuckle.AspNetCore"},{"tags":["javascript"],"question_score":60,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":12,"is_answered":true,"question_id":21926083,"item_type":"question","score":60,"last_activity_date":1725465640,"creation_date":1392960823,"body":"I&#39;m using http://alexgorbatchev.com/SyntaxHighlighter/ to highlight code on my website but sometimes in my log im getting Javascript errors like this :\n\nUncaught NotFoundError: Failed to execute &#39;removeChild&#39; on &#39;Node&#39;: The node to be removed is no longer a child of this node. Perhaps it was moved in a &#39;blur&#39; event handler?\nUncaught NotFoundError: An attempt was made to reference a Node in a context where it does not exist.\n\n\nHere is the attachEvent() function code :\n\nCan anyone help getting this fixed ?\n","excerpt":"I&#39;m using http://alexgorbatchev.com/SyntaxHighlighter/ to highlight code on my website but sometimes in my log im getting Javascript errors like this :\n\nUncaught NotFoundError: Failed to execute &#39;remo &hellip; ","title":"Failed to execute &#39;removeChild&#39; on &#39;Node&#39;"},{"tags":["java","spring-boot","swagger","swagger-ui"],"question_score":-1,"is_accepted":false,"answer_id":78917586,"is_answered":false,"question_id":78916317,"item_type":"answer","score":0,"last_activity_date":1724937037,"creation_date":1724743195,"body":"It seems springdoc has only syntaxHighlight config for speeding up ui, as it&#39;s not helping i can suggest:\n\nWrite custom OpenApiCustomizer bean, override customise(OpenAPI openApi) method, like this\n\n\n\nIf the problem is only in UI and not in swagger json/yaml file, you can customize ui css and js, example is here\nhttps://github.com/springdoc/springdoc-openapi/issues/737\nIt&#39;s somewhat hacky, but can help\n\nWrite an issue on https://github.com/springdoc/springdoc-openapi, suggest solution, or write one yourself\n\n\n","excerpt":"It seems springdoc has only <span class=\"highlight\">syntaxHighlight</span> config for speeding up ui, as it&#39;s not helping i can suggest:\n\nWrite custom OpenApiCustomizer bean, override customise(OpenAPI openApi) method, like this\n\n@Override &hellip; ","title":"How to prevent Swagger from crashing when receiving huge responses?"},{"tags":["java","spring-boot","swagger","swagger-ui"],"question_score":-1,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":false,"question_id":78916317,"item_type":"question","score":-1,"last_activity_date":1724937037,"creation_date":1724706878,"body":"Swagger continually crashes when trying out endpoints with large responses.\nWe have tried disabling syntax highlighting to reduce filesize but still ran into issue.\nSpring configs to remove syntax highlight:\n\nWe are using SpringBoot 3.\nAre there any known ways to have swagger only return file as a downloadable without preview or allow larger sized api responses?\n","excerpt":"Spring configs to remove syntax highlight:\nspringdoc:\n    swagger-ui:\n        <span class=\"highlight\">syntaxHighlight</span>:\n            activated: false\n\nWe are using SpringBoot 3. &hellip; ","title":"How to prevent Swagger from crashing when receiving huge responses?"},{"tags":["c#","ide","editor","syntax-highlighting","abstract-syntax-tree"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":false,"answer_id":78761532,"is_answered":false,"question_id":78760791,"item_type":"answer","score":0,"last_activity_date":1721706235,"creation_date":1721248753,"body":"Writing a syntax parser is meta-djin thinking and the ultimate case of Hofstadter&#39;s law, especially for HTML :)\nHere&#39;s a few pointers, having wrote both token-based and regex-based parsers (and syntax declaration parsers) in different languages and stacks (say desktop vs. web/cloud).\n\nYou&#39;re writing a state machine regardless of your parsing preference, and even before the user presses another key, never mind copying &amp; pasting blocks of code. That means you need strategies for current state (at rest) and for each event or type of event.\nRegex-pattern (pun intended) does get you into performance considerations as explained in Interpreted vs. source-generated vs. compiled regular expressions. The learning curve is steeper, but patterns achieve greater encapsulation in syntax rules (another object in your model).\nThe token-based approach is for single-character tokens (ahem, tokens). It is fast, but it multiplies states sensibly and makes it harder to express and/or interpret syntax rules.\nDon&#39;t append to a string, use a string builder instead.\nThe state machine is a giant switch onion that layers spans with styles, say, if &#39;&lt;&#39; push a tag span to the stack at that position, if &#39;=&#39; push the equal span and if &#39;&gt;&#39; close the span, and so on. This is faster than traversing your dictionary keys.\nThere&#39;s quite a few open-source highlighters out there; do reinvent the wheel if you aim to learn, do not if you have a timeline and a paycheck associated to this :). The ultimate C# full blown code base is Avalon Edit, and I&#39;ve written extensively about a simple HTML/JS/CSS OOP approach (with working samples) at github/hectorjrivas/syntaxhighlighting.\n\n","excerpt":"Writing a syntax parser is meta-djin thinking and the ultimate case of Hofstadter&#39;s law, especially for HTML :)\nHere&#39;s a few pointers, having wrote both token-based and regex-based parsers (and syntax &hellip; ","title":"How to implement text highlighting in a console text editor C#"},{"tags":["reactjs","typescript","next.js","react-markdown","react-syntax-highlighter"],"question_score":2,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":2,"is_answered":true,"question_id":69848211,"item_type":"question","score":2,"last_activity_date":1717821255,"creation_date":1636081001,"body":"I&#39;m following the Github https://github.com/remarkjs/react-markdown and am trying to add SyntaxHighlighter to my markdown code snippets. I&#39;m getting an error mentioned below when trying to use the example code inside a function which I use to render the posts. Markdown is using three backticks and this uses NextJS.\nIf I comment out the line  the red underline is removed but I dont see the code taking effect in my posts\nTried adding any as below but still I dont see any effect in the markdown.\n\nError:\n\nCode:\n\n\n","excerpt":"I&#39;m following the Github https://github.com/remarkjs/react-markdown and am trying to add SyntaxHighlighter to my markdown code snippets. I&#39;m getting an error mentioned below when trying to use the exa &hellip; ","title":"Using syntax highlighter with tsx react markdown"},{"tags":["javascript","html","css","syntax-highlighting","highlight.js"],"question_score":1,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":0,"is_answered":false,"question_id":78510344,"item_type":"question","score":1,"last_activity_date":1716312010,"creation_date":1716277724,"body":"According to official documentation, syntaxhightlight version 11 remove useBR configuration.\nIt recommend to use plugin or simply css \nI can do it with plugin like this.\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\nHow to do it with simply css  ?\n","excerpt":"According to official documentation, syntaxhightlight version 11 remove useBR configuration.\nIt recommend to use plugin or simply css white-space:pre\nI can do it with plugin like this.\n\r\n\r\n&lt;!doctype h &hellip; ","title":"Use css whitespace in pre code syntaxhighlight version 11"},{"tags":["reactjs","markdown","react-markdown","react-syntax-highlighter"],"question_score":5,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":2,"is_answered":true,"question_id":71907116,"item_type":"question","score":5,"last_activity_date":1713978044,"creation_date":1650250138,"body":"I&#39;m building a blog with ReactMarkdown, and I want to render a custom component for the code blocks:\n\nMy &#39;PrismHighlighter&#39; file consists in the following:\n\nThe problem is the following: ReactMarkdown is receiving a string (what is okay), like this:\n\n\n\nBut ReactMarkdown sends to PrismHighlighter an array of objects, like this:\nexample of what ReactMarkdown sends\nThis results of PrismHighlighter avoiding several lines and showing only half or less of the code, like this:\nexample\nSo, does anyone knows what happening here? I&#39;m struggling with this for days now.\n","excerpt":"PrismHighlighter&#39; file consists in the following:\nimport { Prism as SyntaxHighlighter } from &#39;react-syntax-highlighter&#39;;\nimport { nightOwl } from &#39;react-syntax-highlighter/dist/cjs/styles/prism&#39;;\n\nconst <span class=\"highlight\">SyntaxHighlight</span> &hellip; = ({ props, children }) =&gt; (\n  &lt;SyntaxHighlighter style={nightOwl} language=&quot;javascript&quot; showLineNumbers {...props}&gt;\n    {children}\n  &lt;/SyntaxHighlighter&gt;\n);\n\nexport default <span class=\"highlight\">SyntaxHighlight</span>;\n\nThe problem &hellip; ","title":"React-markdown and react-syntax-highlighter"},{"tags":["configuration","astrojs"],"question_score":1,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":true,"answer_count":2,"is_answered":true,"question_id":78022593,"item_type":"question","score":1,"last_activity_date":1713217635,"creation_date":1708364610,"body":"I am trying to add  to my astro project. Whatever I try to do I can not get the example to work.\n\nI have to following dependencies:\n\nAnd the following config:\n\nI ue the configuration as described in the astro documentation but no luck.\nIn the rendered output I get\n\n","excerpt":"const isProduction = process.env.NODE_ENV === &#39;production&#39;;\n\n// https://astro.build/config\nexport default defineConfig({\n  site: &quot;https://www.sanderboer.nl/&quot;,\n  prefetch: true,\n  markdown: {\n    <span class=\"highlight\">syntaxHighlight</span> &hellip; ","title":"astro shikiji transformers not being applied on mdx content"},{"tags":["wordpress","markdown","syntax-highlighting"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":true,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":true,"question_id":34710815,"item_type":"question","score":0,"last_activity_date":1710732645,"creation_date":1452460407,"body":"There are several tags used for code syntax highlighters, such as  and . How to make them compatible at the same site?\n\n\n\nPS: I install the plugin SyntaxHighlighter Evolved, use PreCode in Windows Live Writer for offline blogging and WP markdown editor for online blogging. \n","excerpt":"There are several tags used for code syntax highlighters, such as pre and code. How to make them compatible at the same site?\n\n# Use PreCode for Windows Live Writer\n&lt;pre class=&quot;brush: py; toolbar: fal &hellip; ","title":"How to make code syntax highlighters compatible?"},{"tags":["javascript","json","pretty-print"],"question_score":3557,"is_accepted":false,"answer_id":67802513,"is_answered":false,"question_id":4810841,"item_type":"answer","score":3,"last_activity_date":1709941669,"creation_date":1622626347,"body":"based on @user123444555621, just slightly more modern.\n\nyou can also specify the colors inside js (no CSS needed)\n\nand a version with less regex\n\n","excerpt":".*/, &quot;number&quot;],\n]\n\nconst <span class=\"highlight\">syntaxHighlight</span> = obj =&gt; JSON.stringify(obj, null, 4)\n    .replace(/&amp;/g, &#39;&amp;amp;&#39;)\n    .replace(/&lt;/g, &#39;&amp;lt;&#39;)\n    .replace(/&gt;/g, &#39;&amp;gt;&#39;)\n    .replace(/(&quot;(\\\\u[a-zA-Z0-9]{4}|\\\\[^u &hellip; specify the colors inside js (no CSS needed)\nconst clsMap = [\n    [/^&quot;.*:$/, &quot;red&quot;],\n    [/^&quot;/, &quot;green&quot;],\n    [/true|false/, &quot;blue&quot;],\n    [/null/, &quot;magenta&quot;],\n    [/.*/, &quot;darkorange&quot;],\n]\n\nconst <span class=\"highlight\">syntaxHighlight</span> &hellip; ","title":"pretty-print JSON using JavaScript"},{"tags":["reactjs","typescript","server-side-rendering","astrojs"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":true,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":false,"question_id":76079755,"item_type":"question","score":0,"last_activity_date":1709384093,"creation_date":1682168251,"body":"So when trying to build the Astro codebase with  I got the following error.\n\nThis is my \n\nAs you can see  is already enabled. I have a component called  as I am trying to create a pdf summarization tool on my website but I am also limiting IP because it&#39;s free.\n\n is a simple react functional component and I have created a backed API \n\nSo this is it, this thing is working with  but when I tried to deploy it on   failed, also I checked if  fails locally or not. It does fail locally as well.\nIf you know of any other configuration I have missed or maybe is it an error because of react component I am using  as well but it didn&#39;t help.\n","excerpt":"import vercel from &quot;@astrojs/vercel/serverless&quot;;\nimport react from &quot;@astrojs/react&quot;;\n\n// https://astro.build/config\nexport default defineConfig({\n  site: &quot;https://visrut.xyz&quot;,\n  markdown: {\n    <span class=\"highlight\">syntaxHighlight</span> &hellip; ","title":"`Astro.clientAddress` is only available when using `output: &#39;server&#39;`. I have added output: &#39;server&#39; already"},{"tags":["reactjs","astrojs"],"question_score":2,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":true,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":true,"question_id":76055053,"item_type":"question","score":2,"last_activity_date":1709160418,"creation_date":1681910572,"body":"This is my simple react component that is fetching the quote on the client side.\n\nThis is my  component, where I have a basic layout and I want to show react component.\n\nI am using  as the docs said but it seems to give me this error\n\nAlthough I gave the value  as well it does not seem to be working I tried changing the file extension from  to  not worked.\nMy  is as follows\n\nMy dependencies in \n\n","excerpt":"astrojs/sitemap&#39;; // https://astro.build/config\n\nimport vercel from &quot;@astrojs/vercel/serverless&quot;;\n\n// https://astro.build/config\nexport default defineConfig({\n  site: &quot;https://url&quot;,\n  markdown: {\n    <span class=\"highlight\">syntaxHighlight</span> &hellip; ","title":"astro hydration strategy `client:only=&quot;react&quot;` not working with react js"},{"tags":["configuration","astrojs"],"question_score":1,"is_accepted":true,"answer_id":78026270,"is_answered":false,"question_id":78022593,"item_type":"answer","score":1,"last_activity_date":1708422585,"creation_date":1708422585,"body":"You need to import the transformer you found in the documentation and pass it to the config:\n\n","excerpt":"documentation and pass it to the config:\nimport { defineConfig } from &quot;astro/config&quot;;\nimport { transformerNotationHighlight } from &#39;shikiji-transformers&#39;;\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  markdown: {\n    <span class=\"highlight\">syntaxHighlight</span> &hellip; ","title":"astro shikiji transformers not being applied on mdx content"},{"tags":["syntax-highlighting","mediawiki"],"question_score":2,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":2,"is_answered":true,"question_id":57297288,"item_type":"question","score":2,"last_activity_date":1704000998,"creation_date":1564599403,"body":"I have a fresh Mediawiki installed into fresh UBUNTU 18 LTS... The &#39;&#39;SyntaxHighlight&#39;&#39; extension not works for Unix shell, , , , ... no one is working. It is not at #Supported_languages, and there are no clues about how to install &quot;Other markup&quot;.\n\nAt mediawiki.org/list there are no clues.\n\nSo, how to solve the problem? It is a config, env or syntax problem?\n\n\n\nNOTES AND TESTS\n\nNotes. \n\n\nIt is a corporative Wiki, no way to offer public URL... But it is a fresh, standard and controlled installation, all reproductive and standard.\nThe Wiki was configured with skin &quot;Vector&quot; and language &quot;Brazilian Portuguese&quot;. \n\n\nTests.\n\n\nUsage tests of mediawiki.org/Extension:SyntaxHighlight, the Python example.\n\n1.1. With tag . Result: no highlight, same as .\n\n1.2. With tag . Result: no highlight, same as .\nPHP example, fragment from wikipedia.org/PHP Syntax.\n\n2.1. With tag . Result: no highlight, same as .\n\n2.2. With tag . Result: no highlight, same as .\n\n\nThe code fragments used in the tests:\n\n\n\n\n","excerpt":"The &#39;&#39;<span class=\"highlight\">SyntaxHighlight</span>&#39;&#39; extension not works for Unix shell, lang=&quot;sh&quot;, lang=&quot;shell&quot;, lang=&quot;bash&quot;, ... no one is working. &hellip; With tag &lt;<span class=\"highlight\">syntaxhighlight</span>&gt;. Result: no highlight, same as &lt;pre&gt;.\n\n2.2. With tag &lt;source&gt;. Result: no highlight, same as &lt;pre&gt;. &hellip; ","title":"How to use correct lang parameter?"},{"tags":["mediawiki"],"question_score":6,"is_accepted":false,"answer_id":75761923,"is_answered":false,"question_id":7583337,"item_type":"answer","score":1,"last_activity_date":1703780124,"creation_date":1679003300,"body":"The solution I got from this answer at Webmasters SE works for me:\n\nAlthough the  tag is deprecated and modern markup should look like this:\n\n\nIf your pre content is code, you can use a language such as  to get syntax highlighting.\n","excerpt":"works for me:\n# Some content\n# &lt;source&gt;\nSome pre-formatted content\n&lt;/source&gt;\n# Some more content\n\nAlthough the &lt;source&gt; tag is deprecated and modern markup should look like this:\n# Some content\n# &lt;<span class=\"highlight\">syntaxhighlight</span> &hellip; &gt;\nSome pre-formatted content\n&lt;/<span class=\"highlight\">syntaxhighlight</span>&gt;\n# Some more content\n\n\nIf your pre content is code, you can use a language such as &lt;<span class=\"highlight\">syntaxhighlight</span> lang=&quot;php&quot;&gt; to get syntax highlighting. &hellip; ","title":"How to embed &lt;pre&gt; tag in a list in a wiki"},{"tags":["gatsby","syntax-highlighting","prismjs","datocms"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":false,"answer_id":77639040,"is_answered":false,"question_id":76668318,"item_type":"answer","score":0,"last_activity_date":1702292039,"creation_date":1702292039,"body":"you are on the right path to achieving syntax highlighting with a StructuredText field. All should work fine if all has been setup correctly.\nHere are two ways I suggest you can use to achieve syntax highlighting. Hopefully it helps you and others with similar issues.\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\n","excerpt":"import { renderNodeRule, StructuredText } from &quot;react-datocms&quot;;\nimport { isCode } from &quot;datocms-structured-text-utils&quot;;\nimport Prism from &quot;prismjs&quot;;\nimport <span class=\"highlight\">SyntaxHighlight</span> from &quot;components/<span class=\"highlight\">SyntaxHighlight</span> &hellip; /&gt;\n            );\n        }),\n\n        // Use a custom syntax highlighter component for code blocks\n        renderNodeRule(isCode, ({ node, key }) =&gt; {\n            return (\n                &lt;<span class=\"highlight\">SyntaxHighlight</span> &hellip; ","title":"Code formating in datoCMS Structured Text in Gatsby"},{"tags":["c#","unity-game-engine","syntax-highlighting","textmeshpro"],"question_score":1,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":true,"question_id":76050809,"item_type":"question","score":1,"last_activity_date":1701022870,"creation_date":1681879240,"body":"Here is the code\n\nI&#39;m trying to make syntaxHighliter in TMP input field, I want for example if I type the word &quot;mov&quot; it immediatly changes color to blue, but here apparently the outputfield.text is not changing when I modify it here. I tried changing directly inputfield but that created an infinite loop, tried modifying input field resulted in an infinite loop\n","excerpt":"Here is the code\nusing System.Collections;\nusing System.Collections.Generic;\nusing UnityEngine;\nusing TMPro;\nusing System.Text.RegularExpressions;\npublic class syntaxHighlter : MonoBehaviour\n{\n    [Se &hellip; ","title":"SyntaxHighlighter in unity"},{"tags":["python","wiki","mediawiki","pywikibot"],"question_score":1,"is_accepted":false,"answer_id":66106848,"is_answered":false,"question_id":1021884,"item_type":"answer","score":0,"last_activity_date":1697797438,"creation_date":1612806989,"body":"Pywikibot is able to remove any wikitext or html tags. There are two functions inside textlib:\n\nremoveHTMLParts\nReturn text without portions where HTML markup is disabled but keeps text between html tags. For example:\n\nthis will print:\n\n\nremoveDisabledParts\nReturn text without portions where wiki markup is disabled. This removes text inside wikitext text. For example:\n\nthis will print:\n\nThere are a lot of predefined tags to be removed or to be kept like\n;\ndefault for tags parameter is \nSome other examples:\n gives \n gives \n gives , but works only for Pywikibot 6.0.0 or higher\n\n\n","excerpt":"is  text\n\nThere are a lot of predefined tags to be removed or to be kept like\n&#39;comment&#39;, &#39;header&#39;, &#39;link&#39;, &#39;template&#39;;\ndefault for tags parameter is [&#39;comment&#39;, &#39;includeonly&#39;, &#39;nowiki&#39;, &#39;pre&#39;, &#39;<span class=\"highlight\">syntaxhighlight</span> &hellip; ","title":"Can I use pywikipedia to get just the text of a page?"},{"tags":["reactjs","codemirror","codemirror-modes","react-codemirror"],"question_score":3,"is_accepted":true,"answer_id":76919714,"is_answered":false,"question_id":76912559,"item_type":"answer","score":1,"last_activity_date":1692260896,"creation_date":1692260896,"body":"I got the same error, i solved it by changing the &#39;syntaxHighlighting&#39; extension:\n\nAnd here is the custom highlight style:\n\nI hope it helps\n","excerpt":"I got the same error, i solved it by changing the &#39;syntaxHighlighting&#39; extension:\nEditorState.create({\n   doc: initialText,\n   extensions: [\n     ...\n     syntaxHighlighting(CUSTOM_HIGHLIGHT_STYLE),\n  &hellip; ","title":"CodeMirror says Unrecognized extension value in extension set"},{"tags":["javascript","reactjs"],"question_score":1,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":true,"question_id":65860867,"item_type":"question","score":1,"last_activity_date":1692095262,"creation_date":1611415098,"body":"I&#39;m using  to write a blog which will contain code blocks (which react-quill supports). I&#39;m saving my blog as a JSON string in my database (mongodb) which I then retrieve on the front end.\nI&#39;m currently using  to render the string which is fine, however I want to throw the code blocks (only the code blocks) into . I&#39;m searched the documentation of react-syntax-highlight and react-render to see if there&#39;s a way I can do this but I&#39;m struggling to find a solution.\nAt present I can either render the entire thing in a code block (including the content that is not code)\n\nOr I can render the entire thing as html, without syntax highlighting.\n\nIs there a way I can selectively apply syntax highlighting to just the  tags of the rendered JSON string? Or a better way I could take this?\nAny help appreciated, thank you!\n","excerpt":"I&#39;m using react-quill to write a blog which will contain code blocks (which react-quill supports). I&#39;m saving my blog as a JSON string in my database (mongodb) which I then retrieve on the front end.\n &hellip; ","title":"React SyntaxHighlighter only on &lt;pre&gt; block"},{"tags":["swagger","swagger-ui","openapi"],"question_score":26,"is_accepted":false,"answer_id":75950582,"is_answered":false,"question_id":63615230,"item_type":"answer","score":2,"last_activity_date":1690537382,"creation_date":1680790617,"body":"The equivalent in spring-boot, if using SpringDoc-openapi, is to add this to your application.yml\n\nHere&#39;s the link to the official docs: https://springdoc.org/#swagger-ui-properties\n","excerpt":"The equivalent in spring-boot, if using SpringDoc-openapi, is to add this to your application.yml\nspringdoc:\n  swagger-ui:\n    <span class=\"highlight\">syntaxHighlight</span>:\n      activated: false\n\nHere&#39;s the link to the official docs &hellip; ","title":"swagger-ui hangs on big responses"},{"tags":["next.js13","mdxjs"],"question_score":1,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":0,"is_answered":false,"question_id":76691490,"item_type":"question","score":1,"last_activity_date":1689375079,"creation_date":1689375079,"body":"I have using nextjs 13.4.4 app directory in my current project, and i have render MDX on my nextjs project, and now I want to render element from MDX after replaching with some data from my mdx-components.tsx file. But unforcunatly I can&#39;t access of any data\nhere&#39;s inside of the code you can see I have try to get h1 element from MDX but It can&#39;t acces anything, and this file is not render anything in browser\n\n","excerpt":"h1: ({ children }) =&gt; &lt;h1&gt; - {children} &lt;/h1&gt;,\n    ...components,\n    // code: <span class=\"highlight\">SyntaxHighlight</span>,\n    // code: <span class=\"highlight\">SyntaxHighlight</span>,\n  };\n} &hellip; ","title":"Nextjs 13, MDX-components file can&#39;t access data"},{"tags":["javascript","reactjs","markdown","syntax-highlighting","react-markdown"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":false,"question_id":76684790,"item_type":"question","score":0,"last_activity_date":1689313535,"creation_date":1689310018,"body":"I am getting data as stream which i pass to ReactMarkdown but somehow it syntax highlight doesnot work. however the same string when completed i pass to ReactMarkdown it is working as expected